Revision under test: working tree based on 34a5012 (latest validator range fix)
Finding: user screenshots show 13-character host Lobby ID beginning E. Host creates a positive 63-bit value; 13-character Base32 uses 3 high bits in the first character, so A through H are valid. Both QR parser and manual lookup had incorrectly limited this to A/B.
Changed: InvitationUri and UI decoder now accept A-H and reject I-Z/2-7 in the first position; manual validation distinguishes length errors from invalid IDs.
